  "notes": [
    "Replace specimen labels in an explicitly reviewed plan when real batch IDs are known; retain material, printer, orientation, dry state and slicer record per specimen.",
    "All limits are prototype development acceptance criteria, not a reliability demonstration or flight qualification.",
    "Test fixtures shall restrain the payload after separation. These instructions do not authorize airborne testing.",
    "Dimensional acceptance is separately listed in the manufacturing inspection table; these tests do not replace it.",
    "Demand force is measured on the assembled keeper under 8.9044 N equivalent 2 g loading, real pads and the actual as-printed interface. Available force is measured at the same output position, commanded speed, supply and duty without relying on stall torque."
